---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro'
import DocsSidebar from '../../components/DocsSidebar.astro'
---
<SiteLayout title="API reference - Open MindMap" description="The Open MindMap v0.9 public component, controller, feature, extension, and export APIs.">
  <div class="shell docs-layout">
    <DocsSidebar active="api" />

    <article class="docs-content">
      <span class="eyebrow">API reference</span>
      <h1>Small entrypoints. Clear contracts.</h1>
      <p>Use the entrypoint that owns the behavior you need. Types below match the v0.9 runtime declarations; optional properties are omitted from the examples only when their defaults are obvious.</p>
      <div class="docs-callout">The root <code>@xiangfa/mindmap</code> export aliases <code>MindMapEditor</code> as <code>MindMap</code>. Use <code>core</code>, <code>static</code>, <code>viewer</code>, <code>editor</code>, <code>features/*</code>, and <code>extensions/*</code> for explicit dependency boundaries.</div>

      <h2 id="api-reference">API reference</h2>
      <div class="docs-table-wrap"><table class="docs-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Entry</th><th>Exports</th><th>Use it for</th><th>Styles</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>@xiangfa/mindmap/core</code></td><td>Document, parser, serializer, layout, patches, controller, stream, SVG, URL, and inline helpers</td><td>Headless or server work</td><td>None</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>@xiangfa/mindmap/static</code></td><td><code>StaticMindMap</code> and core types</td><td>Deterministic mounted SVG</td><td><code>styles/static.css</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>@xiangfa/mindmap/viewer</code></td><td><code>MindMapViewer</code> and core types</td><td>Read-only pan, zoom, selection, and folding</td><td><code>styles/viewer.css</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>@xiangfa/mindmap/editor</code></td><td><code>MindMapEditor</code>, editor props/refs, Feature types, and core types</td><td>Editing surface</td><td><code>styles/editor.css</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>@xiangfa/mindmap/features/*</code></td><td>History, search, import, export, Markdown editor, and AI Features</td><td>Opt-in editor capabilities</td><td>Feature stylesheet when provided</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>@xiangfa/mindmap/extensions/*</code></td><td>Syntax and layout Extension factories</td><td>Opt-in Markdown behavior</td><td>None</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>

      <h3>Common inputs</h3>
      <p>All three surfaces can receive a <code>MindMapDocument</code>, a single <code>MindMapNode</code> or node array through <code>data</code>, or Markdown through <code>markdown</code>. Viewer and Editor also accept <code>defaultMarkdown</code>. Without an external controller, multiple sources resolve in this order: <code>document</code>, then <code>data</code>, then <code>markdown</code>, then <code>defaultMarkdown</code>; keep one source controlled so host updates remain unambiguous. An external <code>controller</code> is the sole content owner and is mutually exclusive with every content Prop and <code>documentRevision</code>.</p>
      <div class="code-block"><pre><code>import &#123; MindMapEditor &#125; from '@xiangfa/mindmap/editor'
import &#123; basicMindMapExtensions &#125; from '@xiangfa/mindmap/extensions'
import '@xiangfa/mindmap/styles/editor.css'

const extensions = basicMindMapExtensions()

&lt;MindMapEditor
  markdown=&#123;markdown&#125;
  extensions=&#123;extensions&#125;
  direction="both"
  theme="auto"
  autoFit="initial"
/&gt;</code></pre></div>

      <h2 id="editor-props">MindMapEditorProps</h2>
      <p><code>MindMapEditor</code> owns the editing surface and accepts the following props.</p>
