      <h3 id="toolbar">MindMapToolbarConfig</h3>
      <div class="code-block"><pre><code>interface MindMapToolbarConfig &#123;
  zoom?: boolean
  history?: boolean
  search?: boolean
  tags?: boolean
  editing?: boolean
  direction?: boolean
  textMode?: boolean
  fullscreen?: boolean
&#125;</code></pre></div>
      <p>Set <code>toolbar=&#123;false&#125;</code> to remove the viewport controls and editor toolbar. An object controls each group while keeping the toolbar mounted.</p>

      <h3 id="commands">Command registry</h3>
      <p>The editor entrypoint also exports <code>MindMapEditorCommand</code>, <code>MindMapCommandContext</code>, <code>MindMapCommandRegistry</code>, and <code>MindMapCommandState</code>. Use <code>createMindMapCommandRegistry</code> for host commands and <code>mindMapTreeMoveCommands</code> for the built-in move and indent command set.</p>
      <div class="code-block"><pre><code>import &#123;
  createMindMapCommandRegistry,
  type MindMapEditorCommand,
&#125; from '@xiangfa/mindmap/editor'

const commands: MindMapEditorCommand[] = [&#123;
  id: 'focus-root',
  label: 'Focus root',
  execute: (&#123; controller &#125;) =&gt; controller.selectNode(controller.getSnapshot().document.roots[0]?.id ?? null),
&#125;]

const registry = createMindMapCommandRegistry(commands, () =&gt; (&#123;
  controller,
  readOnly: false,
&#125;))
await registry.invoke('focus-root')</code></pre></div>

