      <h2 id="data-model">Document and Node model</h2>
      <div class="code-block"><pre><code>interface MindMapNode &#123;
  id: string
  text: string
  children?: MindMapNode[]
  attributes?: MindMapNodeAttributes
&#125;

interface MindMapDocument &#123;
  roots: MindMapNode[]
  direction?: 'left' | 'right' | 'both'
  theme?: 'light' | 'dark' | 'auto'
  metadata?: Record&lt;string, string&gt;
  comments?: &#123; text: string; afterNodeId: string | null &#125;[]
&#125;

interface MindMapNodeAttributes &#123;
  task?: &#123; status: 'todo' | 'doing' | 'done' &#125;
  remark?: &#123; text: string &#125;
  tags?: &#123; values: string[] &#125;
  folding?: &#123; collapsed: boolean &#125;
  multiline?: &#123; lines: string[] &#125;
  connection?: &#123; dotted?: boolean; label?: string &#125;
  [namespace: string]: unknown
&#125;</code></pre></div>
      <p>Node IDs are used by selection, layout indexes, cross-links, and patches. Treat the Document and controller snapshots returned by the runtime as read-only values.</p>

      <h2 id="input-boundaries">Input and image boundaries</h2>
      <p>Every public Document entry validates before cloning, traversal, layout, rendering, patch application, or resolver callbacks. Markdown and aggregate Document content are limited to 1,000,000 UTF-16 code units, with at most 20,000 nodes and 256 nesting levels. IDs, metadata, comments, attributes, tags, multiline lines, cross-links, inline tokens, images, render primitives, and direct patch batches have exported <code>MAX_MINDMAP_*</code> limits. See the <a href="/docs/syntax/#basic-syntax">syntax guide</a> for the complete table.</p>
      <p>Remote HTTP(S) images are denied by default and render as alt text. Set <code>remoteImagePolicy</code> to a predicate for an origin allowlist, or to <code>"allow"</code> only when every sanitized remote URL is trusted. A surface inherits its external controller's policy unless the surface Prop overrides it. Raster data URLs remain available within the input limits.</p>

      <h2 id="events">Callbacks and interaction events</h2>
      <p>Document callbacks carry live Document updates. <code>onEvent</code> carries controller events with previous and current snapshots. <code>onInteractionEvent</code> carries surface commands such as selection, direction, viewport, and fullscreen changes; the Editor also emits search, import, history, and text-mode events. Both surfaces expose dedicated selection or viewport callbacks. The controlled echo guard covers the active transaction and the most recently completed edit or transaction, so a callback echo is not applied as a new edit. Advance <code>documentRevision</code> only for an explicit host replacement; ordinary callback echoes should not reset the controller. When replaying older echoes, sequence them with a new revision.</p>
      <div class="docs-table-wrap"><table class="docs-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Event type</th><th>Payload</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>nodeSelect</code></td><td><code>nodeId: string | null</code></td><td>Editor or Viewer interaction event; Viewer also exposes <code>onSelectedNodeChange</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>nodeFocus</code></td><td><code>nodeId: string</code></td><td>Editor ref or search focus</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>searchChange</code></td><td><code>query, matchCount</code></td><td>Editor Search Feature</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>tagFilterChange</code></td><td><code>tags: string[]</code></td><td>Editor tag filter</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>modeChange</code></td><td><code>mode: 'view' | 'text'</code></td><td>Editor Markdown editor toggle</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>zoomChange</code></td><td><code>zoom: number</code></td><td>Editor or Viewer interaction event; both surfaces expose <code>onViewportChange</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>fullscreenChange</code></td><td><code>fullscreen: boolean</code></td><td>Editor or Viewer fullscreen control</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>undo</code> / <code>redo</code></td><td><code>canUndo, canRedo</code></td><td>Editor History Feature</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>import</code></td><td><code>source, document</code></td><td>Editor Import Feature</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>

      <h3 id="event-phases">Controller event phases</h3>
      <p>Use the phase to distinguish a live document frame from the history commit that should be persisted. Selection and layout-only updates have no Document patch.</p>
      <div class="docs-table-wrap"><table class="docs-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Phase</th><th>When it fires</th><th>Persistence guidance</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>preview</code></td><td>Each live patch in an active transaction or Markdown stream</td><td>Update a preview; do not create a second history record</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>commit</code></td><td>A successful transaction, immediate edit, history command, or authoritative replacement</td><td>Use this phase for commit-only persistence</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>rollback</code></td><td>Transaction cancellation or failure restores the baseline</td><td>Discard preview state and reconcile to <code>current.document</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>change</code></td><td>Selection or layout-only state changes</td><td>Keep it out of Document history</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>

      <h2 id="controller">Controller and stream</h2>
      <p>The headless controller owns Document changes, selection, layout options, transactions, and history. The Markdown stream is an incremental source that can be committed through the controller.</p>
      <div class="code-block"><pre><code>import &#123;
  createMarkdownStream,
  createMindMapController,
  parseMindMap,
  serializeMindMap,
&#125; from '@xiangfa/mindmap/core'

const document = parseMindMap('Roadmap\n- Research')
const controller = createMindMapController(document)
const stream = controller.createMarkdownStream()

stream.append('\n- Delivery')
await stream.commit()
const markdown = serializeMindMap(controller.getSnapshot().document)</code></pre></div>
      <p>Controller methods include <code>setDocument</code>, <code>replaceDocument</code>, <code>setMarkdown</code>, <code>applyPatches</code>, <code>selectNode</code>, <code>setDirection</code>, <code>updateNode</code>, <code>insertNode</code>, <code>removeNode</code>, <code>moveNode</code>, <code>toggleFold</code>, <code>beginTransaction</code>, <code>createMarkdownStream</code>, <code>undo</code>, and <code>redo</code>.</p>

      <h2 id="i18n">i18n and messages</h2>
      <p>The runtime detects <code>navigator.language</code> when <code>locale</code> is omitted and provides English (<code>en-US</code>) and Simplified Chinese (<code>zh-CN</code>) message sets. Pass a locale or a partial message object to override selected labels.</p>
      <div class="code-block"><pre><code>import &#123; detectLocale, resolveMessages &#125; from '@xiangfa/mindmap'

const locale = detectLocale()
const messages = resolveMessages('en-US', &#123;
  generate: 'Map it',
  close: 'Dismiss',
&#125;)

&lt;MindMapEditor locale="en-US" messages=&#123;messages&#125; /&gt;</code></pre></div>
      <p>Message keys cover viewport controls, editing, context menus, import/export, history, search, tags, AI, and shared close/cancel actions. Use <code>Partial&lt;MindMapMessages&gt;</code> so the runtime supplies the remaining labels.</p>

      <h2 id="keyboard-shortcuts">Keyboard shortcuts</h2>
      <p>Editor commands apply when the surface has focus. Inputs, textareas, selects, links, and buttons keep their native editing behavior. Viewer supports navigation, folding, fitting, panning, and zooming without editor mutations.</p>
      <div class="docs-table-wrap"><table class="docs-table docs-table--wide">
        <thead><tr><th>Shortcut or gesture</th><th>Editor</th><th>Viewer</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Arrow keys</td><td>Move selection to parent, child, or sibling</td><td>Move selection through the semantic tree</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Tab</code></td><td>Add a child to the selected node</td><td>—</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Shift + Enter</code></td><td>Add a sibling after the selected node</td><td>—</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Enter</code> or <code>F2</code></td><td>Edit the selected node</td><td>—</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Delete</code> or <code>Backspace</code></td><td>Remove the selected node</td><td>—</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Escape</code></td><td>Clear selection or close the current edit path</td><td>—</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Space</code></td><td>Toggle the selected node's folding state</td><td>Toggle the selected node's folding state</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Cmd/Ctrl + Z</code></td><td>Undo</td><td>—</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Cmd/Ctrl + Shift + Z</code> or <code>Cmd/Ctrl + Y</code></td><td>Redo</td><td>—</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Cmd/Ctrl + C/X/V</code></td><td>Copy, cut, or paste a subtree</td><td>—</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Shift + 0</code></td><td>Fit the map to the viewport</td><td>Fit the map to the viewport</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Shift + L/R/M</code></td><td>Set left, right, or both-side direction</td><td>Set left, right, or both-side direction</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Alt + Arrow</code></td><td>Move or reparent the selected node</td><td>—</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Scroll wheel</td><td>Zoom around the pointer</td><td>Zoom around the pointer</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Click-drag empty canvas</td><td>Pan</td><td>Pan</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Click-drag a node</td><td>Place before, after, or under a target node</td><td>—</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Right-click a node</td><td>Open the context menu</td><td>—</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>

      <h2 id="utility-functions">Utility functions</h2>
      <p>Use the explicit public names below for headless parsing, layout, serialization, export, and safe input handling.</p>
      <div class="docs-table-wrap"><table class="docs-table docs-table--wide">
        <thead><tr><th>Entry</th><th>Functions and types</th><th>Use</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>@xiangfa/mindmap/core</code></td><td><code>parseMindMap</code>, <code>createMindMapParser</code>, <code>serializeMindMap</code></td><td>Parse and round-trip Markdown</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>@xiangfa/mindmap/core</code></td><td><code>layoutMindMap</code>, <code>measureMindMapNodeContent</code></td><td>Project nodes and measure content</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>@xiangfa/mindmap/core</code></td><td><code>applyMindMapPatches</code>, <code>applyMindMapPatchesWithInverse</code>, <code>diffMindMapDocuments</code></td><td>Apply or compare Document changes</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>@xiangfa/mindmap/core</code></td><td><code>createMindMapController</code>, <code>createMarkdownStream</code></td><td>Own transactions, subscriptions, and incremental input</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>@xiangfa/mindmap/core</code></td><td><code>renderMindMapToSvg</code></td><td>Produce standalone SVG without React</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>@xiangfa/mindmap/core</code></td><td><code>tokenizeMindMapInline</code>, <code>sanitizeMindMapUrl</code>, <code>authorizeMindMapImageUrl</code>, <code>MindMapRemoteImagePolicy</code></td><td>Shared inline tokens and explicit remote-image policy</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>@xiangfa/mindmap/core</code></td><td><code>MAX_MINDMAP_*</code> constants</td><td>Hard Document, record, image, and patch limits</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>@xiangfa/mindmap/core</code></td><td><code>normalizeDocument</code>, <code>validateMindMapDocument</code>, <code>freezeDocument</code>, <code>reconcileMindMapIds</code>, <code>walkNodes</code>, <code>findNode</code></td><td>Validate, own, reconcile, and inspect Documents</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>@xiangfa/mindmap/features/export</code></td><td><code>prepareMindMapSvg</code>, <code>renderSvgToPng</code>, <code>exportMindMapOutline</code>, <code>downloadMindMapFile</code>, export limits</td><td>Host-authorized SVG, PNG, outline, and download work</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>@xiangfa/mindmap/editor</code></td><td><code>createMindMapCommandRegistry</code>, <code>mindMapTreeMoveCommands</code>, and command types</td><td>Register host commands and inspect command availability</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>@xiangfa/mindmap</code></td><td><code>detectLocale</code>, <code>resolveMessages</code></td><td>Resolve UI language and overrides</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>
      <div class="code-block"><pre><code>import &#123;
  layoutMindMap,
  parseMindMap,
  renderMindMapToSvg,
  serializeMindMap,
&#125; from '@xiangfa/mindmap/core'
import &#123;
  prepareMindMapSvg,
  renderSvgToPng,
&#125; from '@xiangfa/mindmap/features/export'

const document = parseMindMap(markdown, &#123; extensions &#125;)
const layout = layoutMindMap(document, &#123; extensions &#125;)
const svg = renderMindMapToSvg(document, &#123; extensions &#125;)
const prepared = await prepareMindMapSvg(document, &#123; extensions &#125;)
const png = await renderSvgToPng(prepared)</code></pre></div>
      <p><code>renderSvgToPng(svg, scale?)</code> defaults to scale <code>2</code> and requires a positive finite value. It rejects raw SVG over 16 MiB before URI encoding. Raster output is reduced as needed to stay within 8,192 pixels per side and 16,777,216 total pixels; remote images must be embedded by an authorized <code>imageResolver</code> during <code>prepareMindMapSvg</code>.</p>
